ONSHELL = r'''- **注 `rem:appO-onshell-unitarity` — 在壳线的两粒子幺正性（$O(g^4)$）** (no tag). For two on-shell external lines (massive scalars or time-like eikonal lines) with exact gluon propagators and a gluon-mass regulator, box plus crossed box obey exact two-particle unitarity at $O(g^4)$, ${\rm Disc}_s({\rm box}+{\rm crossed})=\int d\Phi_2\,T_1^\dagger T_1$, by Cutkosky's rules graph by graph (`Cutkosky1960`, `Veltman1963`, `tHooftVeltman1974`): the crossed box has no $s$-channel cut (it would need an on-shell emission from an on-shell massive line), three-particle cuts appear only at $O(g^6)$, and in the high-energy limit $p_{\rm opp}$ is purely imaginary (`prop:dy-eikonal-twogluon`) — the strict-window residual is not a property of the exact graphs (known in substance). For three on-shell lines $(i;j_1;j_2)$ the analogous relation suggests $W_{12}+W_{21}^*=1$, i.e. no half-coincident residual, but a complete argument must include the graphs that combine an $(i$–$j_e)$ exchange with a $(j_1$–$j_2)$ exchange (same colour structure) — open, not certified.'''

